{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ZBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ZBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.utilde_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.utilde_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L377-L385","doc":"**`ũ = q·u` is exactly bar-EVEN (twist `1`), division-free over any\n`CommRing`.** With `u = b·(1 − qi)²`, its bar image is `b·(1 − q)²`, and\n`bar(ũ) = qi·b·(1 − q)² = q·b·(1 − qi)² = ũ`. Contrast `hbar_sq_bar_even_twist`\n/ §8 (`u` alone carries the degree-`q²` twist): multiplying by the single\n`q` cancels it exactly. This is the Lean handle for the ai81/08ds\neven-channel ladder-variable re-normalization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uPow_bar_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uPow_bar_twist","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L349-L354","doc":"**`u`-monomial twist.** If `u'` is the bar-image of the ladder variable\nwith `u' = t·u` (here `t = q²` from `bar(u) = q²·u`), then `u'^k = t^k·u^k`.\nThe twist `t^k = q^{2k}` is degree-dependent (a scaling), in contrast to\nthe constant / Gauss-sum twists of the `q`-side bases (KC12/KC16). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.pochNum_bar_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.pochNum_bar_twist","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L315-L335","doc":"**Index-alternating bar-parity of the Habiro basis (division-free).**\n`pochNum k qi · q^{∑_{j<k}(j+1)} = (−1)^k · pochNum k q` — the basis\nelement `(q;q)_k` is bar-even for even `k`, bar-odd for odd `k`, up to\nthe Gauss-sum monomial twist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.pochFactor_bar_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.pochFactor_bar_twist","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L309-L313","doc":"**Factor twist:** `(1 − q⁻ʲ)·qʲ = −(1 − qʲ)` (division-free: `q·qi = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.pochNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.pochNum","kind":"def","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L305-L307","doc":"`pochNum k q = ∏_{j=1}^k (1 − q^j)` — the one-sided q-Pochhammer\nnumerator `(q;q)_k` over a generic commutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cycFactor_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cycFactor_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L285-L293","doc":"**The cyclotomic factor is exactly bar-invariant** — applying the bar swap\n`(q, x) ↦ (qi, xi)` returns the same element, with no hypotheses at all\n(pure symmetry of the expression). Hence every Habiro basis element `ω_k`\n(a product of such factors) is exactly bar-even, and the 4₁ element with\n`C_k ≡ 1` is bar-even in this basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.cycFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.cycFactor","kind":"def","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L282-L283","doc":"The 4₁ cyclotomic factor `x + x⁻¹ − q^j − q^{−j}` in the pair encoding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.shadow_carried_by_even_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.shadow_carried_by_even_part","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L259-L270","doc":"**Shadow gates test the even part.** For the bar-decomposition\n`a = e + o` (`σ e = e`, `σ o = −o`), every bar-compatible evaluation `φ`\ninto a target where `2` is regular satisfies `φ(a) = φ(e)`: the q=1\nshadow of a kernel coefficient is carried entirely by its bar-even part.\n(Stated over a `Field` target with `(2 : S) ≠ 0` for the cancellation.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.fixed_eval_two_mul_kills_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.fixed_eval_two_mul_kills_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L245-L257","doc":"**A bar-compatible evaluation kills bar-odd elements.** If `φ` is a ring\nhom with `φ ∘ σ = φ` (e.g. evaluation at the bar-fixed point `q = 1`) and\n`σ o = −o`, then `2·φ(o) = 0` — division-free form; over a target of\ncharacteristic ≠ 2 this is `φ(o) = 0`. This is the T3-2 tension made\nprecise: an exactly-bar-odd `a₁` cannot carry the nonzero q=1 shadow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bar_even_ne_bar_odd_of_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bar_even_ne_bar_odd_of_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L221-L231","doc":"**The exclusion (`Field` form): a bar-even scalar cannot equal a bar-odd\nNONZERO element in characteristic ≠ 2.** Applied to the keystone: every\nscalar functional of `z` alone is bar-even (§1 + §4 closure), while the\nkernel's leading coefficient `a₁ = −c₃` is bar-odd\n(`QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.ck_a1_bar_odd_of_c3_odd`) and empirically\nnonzero — so `a₁` is NOT a scalar functional of `z` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bar_even_and_odd_two_mul_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bar_even_and_odd_two_mul_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L214-L219","doc":"**The exclusion, division-free.** An element that is simultaneously\nbar-even and bar-odd satisfies `2·a = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bar_even_mul_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bar_even_mul_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L208-L212","doc":"A bar-EVEN scalar times a bar-ODD element is bar-ODD: multiplying by\nz-functionals never changes parity — the odd channel must be supplied by\nthe carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bar_fixed_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bar_fixed_pow","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L203-L206","doc":"Bar-fixed elements are closed under powers: every monomial `zᵐ` of a\nbar-even atom is bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bar_fixed_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bar_fixed_mul","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L199-L201","doc":"Bar-fixed elements are closed under multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bar_fixed_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bar_fixed_add","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L195-L197","doc":"Bar-fixed elements are closed under addition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.kappa21_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.kappa21_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L179-L189","doc":"**`κ_{(2,1)}` is exactly bar-ODD (division-free, over any `CommRing`).**\nCross-multiplied form of `κ(q⁻¹) = −κ(q)` for\n`κ(q) = (q−1)³(q+1)/q²`: the Lean certificate of the sympy-exact\n`bar(κ)+κ = 0` in the 2026-06-13 heat f-map audit §1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.kappaDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.kappaDen","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L176-L177","doc":"Denominator of the (2,1)-block heat carrier: `q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.kappaNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.kappaNum","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L173-L174","doc":"Numerator of the (2,1)-block heat carrier: `(q−1)³(q+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hbar_sq_bar_even_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hbar_sq_bar_even_twist","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L159-L169","doc":"**`ℏ_q²` is bar-EVEN up to the monomial twist `q²`.** Squaring\n`hbar_bar_odd_twist`: `bar(ℏ²) = q²·ℏ²`. Hence the ladder variable\n`u = b·ℏ_q²` (with `b` a bar-fixed constant) is bar-even up to `q²` —\ninteger `u`-rungs carry even bar-parity content, and any bar-ODD ladder\ncoefficient must be sourced by a genuinely bar-odd carrier, not by the\nvariable itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hbar_bar_odd_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hbar_bar_odd_twist","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L152-L157","doc":"**`ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹` is bar-ODD up to the monomial twist `−q`.** In the\n`(q, qi)` encoding (`q·qi = 1`, `ℏ = 1 − qi`, `bar(ℏ) = 1 − q`):\n`bar(ℏ) = −q·ℏ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_core_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_core_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L136-L147","doc":"**The sharp form: `q⁻²·z_D` IS exactly bar-even (twist `1`).** Since\n`q⁻²·z_D = q/(q²+1) = 1/[2]_q`, the canonical parameter factors as\n`z_D = q² · (bar-even core)`. Division-free cross-multiplied statement:\n`ζ(q) = q/(q²+1)` satisfies `ζ(q⁻¹) = ζ(q)`.\n\nSo D's parity defect is carried entirely by an explicit `q²`, not by the\ncore — which is what makes the twist exponent `−4` in `zD_bar_twist`\n(`−4 = −2·2`) rather than an unstructured function of `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_bar_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_bar_twist","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L119-L134","doc":"**`z_D` is bar-even only up to the monomial twist `q⁻⁴` — it is NOT\nbar-invariant.** Division-free over any `CommRing`, in the `(q, qi)`\nencoding (`q·qi = 1`): the cross-multiplied form of `z_D(q⁻¹) = q⁻⁴·z_D(q)`.\n\n**This is the statement that breaks KC13's transfer.** §1's `Z2` exclusion\n— no scalar rational function of `z` alone can source the bar-ODD channel —\nruns through \"the bar-fixed locus is a subring and `z` lies in it\"\n(`bar_fixed_add` / `bar_fixed_mul` / `bar_fixed_pow`). Under D, `z_D` is\n**not** bar-fixed, so it is not in that subring and the argument does not\napply. Re-examination under D is open (bean `qou-cds1`); the C exclusion is\n**not** evidence about the canonical convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zDDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zDDen","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L115-L117","doc":"Denominator of the canonical convention-D Markov parameter:\n`zDDen q = q² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zDNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zDNum","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L111-L113","doc":"Numerator of the **canonical convention-D** Markov parameter\n`z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.z_bar_invariant_field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.z_bar_invariant_field","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L91-L102","doc":"`Field` corollary of `z_bar_invariant` in literal `a/b` form. Only\n`s ≠ 0` is needed: when `1 + s² = 0` both sides are `0` under Mathlib's\ndivision convention, so the identity is unconditional in the\ndenominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.z_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.z_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L79-L89","doc":"**`z_C` is exactly bar-EVEN (division-free, over any `CommRing`).** 🛑 A\nstatement about the **excised convention C** only — `bar(z_D) = q⁻⁴·z_D`,\nsee `zD_bar_twist` in §1b. Under the\nbar involution `s ↦ s⁻¹` — witnessed by `s·si = 1` — the cross-multiplied\nidentity `zNum si · zDen s = zNum s · zDen si` holds, i.e. `z(s⁻¹) = z(s)`\nwith twist exactly `1`. In `q`-language: `z(q⁻¹) = z(q)` for\n`z = √q/(1+q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zCDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zCDen","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L75-L77","doc":"Denominator of the **convention-C** Markov parameter: `zCDen s = 1 + s²`\n(`= 1 + q`). **Excised convention** — see §1b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zCNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zCNum","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ZBarParity.lean#L70-L73","doc":"Numerator of the **convention-C** Markov parameter `z_C = √q/(1+q)` in the\nhalf-power coordinate `s` (`s² = q`): `zCNum s = s`. **Excised convention** —\nthe canonical parameter is `zDNum`/`zDDen` in §1b. ","signatureChunk":0}]}